# .azure is not intended to be committed
*

# Two deliberate exceptions to azd's blanket rule above.
#
# `*` is right for environment state: `citadel-ui-dev/` holds subscription ids
# and provisioning outputs, and none of that belongs in a repository. But it also
# swallowed the deployment plan, which is the opposite kind of file -- a reviewed
# document, and the artifact azure-prepare, azure-validate and azure-deploy all
# read from disk. Losing it to a wildcard would be silent, and would only be
# noticed by someone who cloned the repo and found no plan.
#
# `.gitignore` itself is re-included so these rules travel with the repository.
# Without it a fresh clone has no ignore file here at all, and the environment
# state this exists to exclude becomes trackable again.
!.gitignore
!deployment-plan.md